{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:BringsSurface.TorusEmbeddableComplete","@type":"LeanModule","name":"BringsSurface.TorusEmbeddableComplete","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Nat.GCD.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.IntervalCases","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.NormNum.Basic"],"declarations":7,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.three_lepton_generations","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.three_lepton_generations","kind":"theorem","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L84-L92","doc":"The completeness is number-theoretic: the Descartes value g = 4\nis the smallest genus accommodating all three lepton generations\nplus a nontrivial quark sector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.no_m_ge_4","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.no_m_ge_4","kind":"theorem","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L72-L82","doc":"No torus knot with m ≥ 4 and m < n satisfies the genus bound. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torus_embeddable_complete","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torus_embeddable_complete","kind":"theorem","line":39,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L39-L70","doc":"**Torus embeddable complete** (Proposition):\n\nT_{m,n} with gcd(m,n) = 1 and 1 < m < n embeds in Σ₄ iff\n(m,n) belongs to the set {(2,3), (2,5), (2,7), (2,9), (3,4), (3,5)}.\n\nProof: The Seifert genus of T_{m,n} is (m-1)(n-1)/2.\nEmbeddability requires (m-1)(n-1) ≤ 8.\n- m = 2: n-1 ≤ 8, n ≤ 9, odd coprime: n ∈ {3,5,7,9}\n- m = 3: 2(n-1) ≤ 8, n ≤ 5, coprime to 3: n ∈ {4,5}\n- m = 4: 3(n-1) ≤ 8, n ≤ 3, but m < n requires n ≥ 5: no solution\n- m ≥ 5: (m-1)(n-1) ≥ 4·m > 8: no solution ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:torus-embeddable-complete","label":"prop:torus-embeddable-complete","md":"quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.embeddablePairs","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.embeddablePairs","kind":"def","line":34,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L34-L37","doc":"The complete list of coprime pairs (m, n) with 1 < m < n and\n(m-1)(n-1) ≤ 8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotEmbeddable","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotEmbeddable","kind":"def","line":29,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L29-L32","doc":"A torus knot T_{m,n} is embeddable in Σ₄ iff g(T_{m,n}) ≤ 4,\ni.e. (m-1)(n-1) ≤ 8. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.torusKnotGenus","kind":"def","line":26,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L26-L27","doc":"Seifert genus of a torus knot T_{m,n}: g = (m-1)(n-1)/2. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.bringsGenus","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.bringsGenus","kind":"def","line":23,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/brings-surface/torus-embeddable-complete.lean#L23-L24","doc":"The genus of the Bring's surface Σ₄. ","signatureChunk":0}]}